shed this SAP ABAP course and agreed to share their story. The salary numbers are what they were actually paid when they got placed. Tap any short to watch. ShortsFresher to 6.5 LPA[ Shorts thumbnail: Akhilesh ]Akhilesh R.ABAP Developer · Infosys Shorts4 → 5.8 LPA[ Shorts thumbnail: Silpa ]Silpa N.ABAP Developer · UST Shorts6 → 11 LPA[ Shorts thumbnail: Mohammed ]Mohammed F.Senior ABAP · Partner ShortsFresher to 5.5 LPA[ Shorts thumbnail: Anjana ]Anjana C.Associate Dev · TCS Want to talk to someone who has done it?Request an alumni call Why now Why SAP ABAP, and why now. Every SAP customisation, report, interface and migration object is written in ABAP, and the S/4HANA wave has created a multi-year backlog of conversion and clean-core development work. ABAP developers are the engine room of that entire migration economy. 2027Conversion deadline drives demandECC-to-S/4HANA conversions need ABAP developers for every custom object. CleanCore: the new skillsetCDS, RAP and released APIs created a modern ABAP profile in short supply. 30yrCareers, still hiringABAP has outlived every obituary; the installed base guarantees decades of work. Why it is a smart move for you A protected developer nicheEnterprise platform skills face far less competition than generic web stacks. Engineering graduates convert fastAny programming logic transfers; the platform depth is what we add. Functional-plus paths openABAP plus FICO or MM knowledge makes the rare, highly paid techno-functional profile. AI raises, not replacesAI drafts boilerplate; developers who know the platform review, integrate and own it. Eligibility Is SAP ABAP right for you? ABAP suits logical minds who enjoy building. Engineering and computer-science backgrounds fast-track; determined graduates from other streams succeed through the logic-first opening modules. A strong fit if you areA B.Tech, BCA, MCA or B.Sc graduate targeting SAP developmentA developer in another stack seeking enterprise stabilityA support consultant moving to developmentA fresher aiming for product-scale enterprise systemsAn SAP functional consultant adding technical depth What you will needA graduate degree, technical preferred10 hours a week for six monthsA laptop; SAP access providedProgramming logic helps; taught if absent [ counsellor photo ]Not sure you qualify?A counsellor reviews your background and tells you honestly. Free, no pressure.Check my eligibility → The full course Curriculum, projects and tools. Week-by-week structure, what past learners built, and every tool you\'ll touch hands-on. Curriculum 10 · Projects 3 · Tools 12. Curriculum 10 Projects 3 Tools 12 M01Programming logic and ABAP first steps24 hrs · Wk 1-3", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Logic refresher: variables, loops, conditionsThe ABAP workbench and repositoryData types and internal tablesYour first reportsDrill: twenty small programs, reviewed"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Is ABAP still worth learning, or is it a dying language?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "The obituary has been wrong for twenty years. The S/4HANA conversion wave through 2027 and beyond created a backlog of ABAP work, and clean-core skills, CDS, RAP, OData, are the modern, in-demand form of it. Installed enterprise bases do not disappear."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Do I need to know programming before joining?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Logic helps but is not required. The first month builds programming thinking deliberately, and engineering graduates fast-track through it. What ABAP demands is care, not prior syntax."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What is modern ABAP versus old ABAP, and which do you teach?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Both, in the right order. Classical ABAP still runs the world\'s systems and interviews; CDS, RAP and OData are where new development happens. You leave able to maintain the old and build the new."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Which 