<div class="faq-wrap">
<div class="acc reveal">
<details open=""><summary>Is ABAP still worth learning, or is it a dying language? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">The obituary has been wrong for twenty years. The S/4HANA conversion wave through 2027 and beyond created a backlog of ABAP work, and clean-core skills, CDS, RAP, OData, are the modern, in-demand form of it. Installed enterprise bases do not disappear.</div></details>
<details><summary>Do I need to know programming before joining? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Logic helps but is not required. The first month builds programming thinking deliberately, and engineering graduates fast-track through it. What ABAP demands is care, not prior syntax.</div></details>
<details><summary>What is modern ABAP versus old ABAP, and which do you teach? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Both, in the right order. Classical ABAP still runs the world's systems and interviews; CDS, RAP and OData are where new development happens. You leave able to maintain the old and build the new.</div></details>
<details><summary>Which certification does this course prepare me for? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">The SAP Certified Associate Back-End Developer for ABAP Cloud (C_ABAPD), with mock exams, plus guidance on the NetWeaver-track alternative. Exams are booked through SAP and charged separately.</div></details>
<details><summary>What is the starting salary for an ABAP developer? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Freshers typically start between Rs 4 and 7 lakh. With a conversion project behind you, Rs 7 to 13 lakh is common, and techno-functional or RAP-fluent seniors climb steeply.</div></details>
<details><summary>ABAP or full stack web development: which should I choose? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Web stacks offer breadth and startup energy; ABAP offers enterprise depth, less competition and the SAP ecosystem's stability. If long platform careers appeal to you, ABAP is the stronger moat.</div></details>
<details><summary>Is it online or classroom, and is Malayalam support available? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Both. In-person batches in Trivandrum, Kochi and Bengaluru, plus live online batches across Kerala, the GCC and beyond. Sessions are in clear English with Malayalam support.</div></details>
<details><summary>Do you guarantee a job after the course? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">No, and we will not pretend otherwise. We provide structured placement support and real introductions across 400+ partners, with support continuing six months after you finish.</div></details>
